WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.741
OpenRouter drops three

00:00:01.553 --> 00:00:02.944
providers after data

00:00:02.756 --> 00:00:03.746
leak findings

00:00:04.278 --> 00:00:05.657
Security researchers

00:00:05.469 --> 00:00:06.459
found some inference

00:00:06.271 --> 00:00:07.485
providers had data

00:00:07.297 --> 00:00:08.759
compromised or weren't

00:00:08.582 --> 00:00:09.537
honoring their data

00:00:09.349 --> 00:00:10.186
policies

00:00:10.325 --> 00:00:11.468
OpenRouter says it

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:12.176
was not breached

00:00:11.987 --> 00:00:12.742
itself

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:14.390
It off-boarded three

00:00:14.202 --> 00:00:15.569
providers and removed

00:00:15.381 --> 00:00:17.715
125 endpoints from

00:00:17.527 --> 00:00:19.001
Zero Data Retention

00:00:18.824 --> 00:00:19.732
eligibility

00:00:19.992 --> 00:00:21.571
then notified potentially

00:00:21.383 --> 00:00:22.656
affected customers

00:00:23.174 --> 00:00:24.435
Next it plans

00:00:24.247 --> 00:00:24.848
to run the

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:25.791
researchers' tests

00:00:25.603 --> 00:00:27.383
continuously and verify

00:00:27.195 --> 00:00:28.398
network paths to

00:00:28.209 --> 00:00:29.789
catch requests forwarded

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:30.827
to third parties

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:32.364
Full story on

00:00:32.175 --> 00:00:33.071
the dashboard
